/T (Filters with real resonators will have insertion loss and finite Q. Real resonators will introduce resistive and parasitic losses and the filter will have lower selectivity. The additional losses result in the widening of the filter bandwidth. When laid out and 3D simulated, crosstalk and other physical effects need to be considered as well.  Many different filter topologies exist; common topologies include: lowpass, highpass, bandpass, notch, and diplexer. The unique filter requirements of a system will dictate which filter topology is the preferred solution. )
