/T (Filter Technologies  Common filter technologies in use today include acoustic wave filters, cavity filters, lumped element filters and planar filters. No single filter technology is best suited to fit all applications; each technology has its own tradeoff space. Cavity filters for example provide excellent out of band rejection, low loss and high power handling at microwave frequencies at the expense of being physically large designs that require hand tuning. Acoustic filters on the other hand offer excellent rejection in a small)
