/T (GaAs fabrication utilizes tightly controlled single crystals that can be produced in high volumes while maintaining repeatability. MMIC filter production is scalable from thousands to millions of units. The fine geometric features available on the process allow for the careful tuning and optimization of features such as transmission zeros via cross-coupling of resonators. These results have been achieved with near perfect match with simulation, enabling first pass design success and a short development cycle.  A tighter tolerance results in better repeatability from unit-to-unit and)
