854 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Modern communication systems require high operating powers to transmit and receive high-bandwidth data. These systems push filter capabilities well beyond 10W for continuous wave operation and 100W for pulsed operating conditions.  The maximum power handling for MMIC filters depends on the topology: filters can have either a RF power handling and/or a max DC current specification. In general, the type of power rating depends on if the input is AC or DC coupled. If the resonator uses a capacitive structure \(or any gaps between conductors\), traces are likely to short when the max power rating is exceeded. For DC coupled inputs, the trace width limits current throughput, and when there is sufficient self-heating, the conductor burns out rendering the through path as an open circuit. For bandpass filters, both max RF power handling and max DC current rating are applicable, but for filter designs that are DC coupled, the max DC current rating will typically be the first to blow. For a subset of MMIC bandpass filters tested so far, typical power handling values have been demonstrated to at least 10W CW so far, though this may vary with)
/E (Modern communication systems require high operating powers to transmit and receive high-bandwidth data. These systems push filter capabilities well beyond 10W for continuous wave operation and 100W for pulsed operating conditions.  The maximum power handling for MMIC filters depends on the topology: filters can have either a RF power handling and/or a max DC current specification. In general, the type of power rating depends on if the input is AC or DC coupled. If the resonator uses a capacitive structure \(or any gaps between conductors\), traces are likely to short when the max power rating is exceeded. For DC coupled inputs, the trace width limits current throughput, and when there is sufficient self-heating, the conductor burns out rendering the through path as an open circuit. For bandpass filters, both max RF power handling and max DC current rating are applicable, but for filter designs that are DC coupled, the max DC current rating will typically be the first to blow. For a subset of MMIC bandpass filters tested so far, typical power handling values have been demonstrated to at least 10W CW so far, though this may vary with)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
