/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (From a dramatic increase in available bandwidth comes an increase in achievable data-rates, making these frequencies extremely interesting to teams around the world working on 5G communications. However, with this increase in frequency comes a set of challenges. The free space path loss \(FSPL\) equation provides a way to calculate signal attenuation through free space or a vacuum. It tells us that signal loss increases as the square of distance and the square of frequency. The higher the frequency the more the signal will degrade over distance, limiting these frequencies to short range and/or high- power communications.)
/E (From a dramatic increase in available bandwidth comes an increase in achievable data-rates, making these frequencies extremely interesting to teams around the world working on 5G communications. However, with this increase in frequency comes a set of challenges. The free space path loss \(FSPL\) equation provides a way to calculate signal attenuation through free space or a vacuum. It tells us that signal loss increases as the square of distance and the square of frequency. The higher the frequency the more the signal will degrade over distance, limiting these frequencies to short range and/or high- power communications.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
